{"id":"g.math.circles.3.b215c58410","section":"math","domain":"geometry","skill":"circles","difficulty":3,"prompt":"The graph of $x^2 + y^2 - 4x - 14y = 47$ in the $xy$-plane is a circle. What is the radius of the circle?","answer":["10"],"explanation":"Complete the square: $(x^2 - 4x + 4) + (y^2 - 14y + 49) = 47 + 4 + 49$, so $(x - 2)^2 + (y - 7)^2 = 100$. The center is $(2, 7)$ and the radius is $10$."},
{"id":"g.math.circles.3.5456355471","section":"math","domain":"geometry","skill":"circles","difficulty":3,"prompt":"The graph of $x^2 + y^2 + 10x + 8y = -16$ in the $xy$-plane is a circle. What is the radius of the circle?","answer":["5"],"explanation":"Complete the square: $(x^2 + 10x + 25) + (y^2 + 8y + 16) = -16 + 25 + 16$, so $(x + 5)^2 + (y + 4)^2 = 25$. The center is $(-5, -4)$ and the radius is $5$."}
